    "body": "### Status\n\nSuperseded by [#8143](https://github.com/verl-project/verl/pull/8143), merged on October 15, 2026, which implements Ascend fused linear cross-entropy through CANN / `torch_npu` and resolves [#7950](https://github.com/verl-project/verl/issues/7950).\n\nThis PR's unconditional Torch fallback would bypass that new CANN path. The original patch should therefore not be merged into current `main`.\n\n### Original change\n\nThe reported Ascend 910B / CANN 9.0 failure occurred when the CUDA-oriented Triton output-head kernel exceeded the device's UB capacity.\n\nThis PR proposed handling an explicit `fused_kernel_options.impl_backend=triton` request by issuing a warning and selecting the native Torch backend when the Ascend runtime is available. It also added configuration documentation and CPU tests for backend selection.\n\n### Validation recorded before the upstream CANN implementation\n\n```bash\nVERL_USE_EXTERNAL_PLUGINS=none PYTHONPATH=. python -m pytest -q \\\n  tests/models/test_fused_kernel_backend_on_cpu.py \\\n  tests/models/test_fused_kernels_ulysses_sp_on_cpu.py \\\n  tests/utils/test_experimental_torch_functional_on_cpu.py\n```\n\nResult: **38 passed** on the original PR revision. Changed-file Ruff checks, documentation date checks, compilation, and `git diff --check` also passed. Ascend 910B / CANN 9.0 execution was not validated locally.\n\nThese results cover the original backend-selection proposal. They do not validate compatibility with the subsequently merged CANN implementation.\n\n### Relationship to the upstream solution\n\n#8143 routes NPU `linear_cross_entropy` to CANN and includes a chunked PyTorch backward path for entropy gradients. It preserves a fused CE execution path on supported NPU installations. This PR's earlier blanket fallback is no longer the appropriate fix for #7950.\n\nAI assistance was used for the implementation, tests, and preparation of this description.\n",
